{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_readme", "label": "Plans README (docs/plans/README.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "header", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_plan_front_matter", "label": "Plan front matter (status/issue/spec/pr)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Naming and front matter", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_plan_lifecycle", "label": "Plan lifecycle (first commit of PR; ready -> in-progress -> done)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Lifecycle", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The plan is committed as the first commit of the ticket's PR so the PR reads spec -> plan -> code; plans are kept forever and done plans stay as portfolio evidence of the workflow."}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_test_first_always", "label": "Test-first, always", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every feature task starts with a failing test: PHPUnit for logic (via the plugin's PHPUnit data generator, tests/generator.php), Behat only for UI journeys; watch the test fail before writing implementation code (superpowers:test-driven-development)."}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_highest_existing_seam", "label": "Highest existing seam", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test through the service classes in classes/, Behat for UI flows; new seams are proposed in the spec (/to-spec step 2), never invented in a plan - the ideal number of new seams is zero."}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_end_of_task_gate", "label": "End-of-task gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every task ends with all of: phpcs at zero findings, user-visible text only via lang strings (get_string(), never hardcoded), a docs/security-checklist.md walk of the task's diff (capability checks, require_sesskey() on writes, required_param/optional_param cleaning), version.php bump + db/upgrade.php savepoint if schema or capabilities changed (CI checks this), and a cache purge via $MOODLE_DOCKER_BIN."}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_name_the_core_api", "label": "Name the core API", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every mechanism in the plan names the Moodle core API it uses, matching the ledger in docs/architecture.md (e.g. grade_update, core_privacy metadata provider); a mechanism with no core API needs an ADR before the plan is written, not during execution - this is the core-API-first principle applied at plan level."}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_tests_generator_php", "label": "tests/generator.php (PHPUnit data generator)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_docs_architecture_md", "label": "docs/architecture.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/README.md", "source_location": "Moodle-specific requirements", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_readme_docs_security_checklist_md", "label": "docs/securit